-The polynomial is continuous on [0,2] and differentiable on (0,2). Its secant slope is $(8-0)/(2-0)=4$. The tangent equation is $3c^2=4$, giving algebraic roots $c=\pm2/\sqrt3$. Only $c=2/\sqrt3$ is positive, and it is below 2 because $\sqrt3>1$; it is therefore the only admissible value. Its tangent is parallel to the endpoint secant. It is not the midpoint 1, whose derivative is 3 rather than 4. Treating c as a midpoint automatically would be an anticipated conceptual mistake; the defining equation and interior restriction determine it here. [Return to P1](#p1) · [Hint P1](#h1)
